      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name may honor Daniel Boone, a friend of Colonel Logan, after whom Logan County is named.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofbooneville.com/local-history",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before settlers, the Osage Indians inhabited the area that is now Booneville, with white settlers arriving in the early 1820s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofbooneville.com/local-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1887 arrival of the Louisiana and San Francisco Railroad linked Booneville to the region, later becoming part of the Rock Island system until 1980.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
